# §0. OPERATOR PROPOSAL — received 2026-07-21 via the AO48 chat line, relayed verbatim

> Recommendation for the Team: Implementing a Dynamic Master Extraction Manifest
> The Issue: Currently, we are managing file tracking through static release indexes (like the C093 inventory). While great for locking down closed environments, this does not give us a live view of our current file delta or status. As we scale the number of isolated theorem folders, manually extracting the finalized proofs for the external referee will become a massive bottleneck.
> We do not have the time to manually audit every folder or become experts in tracking the status of every single mathematical derivation across the entire drive. We need a system that automatically finds the patterns, tracks what works, and logs the solutions so we can simply move forward with the research.
> The Proposal: The Automated Master Manifest
> We need to implement a continuous ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) pipeline for our workspace now, rather than waiting for the end of the project. I recommend we deploy a WORKSPACE_MASTER_MANIFEST.json governed by a lightweight orchestration script.
> How it works:
> 1. Automated Indexing: A script runs continuously (or on a nightly cron job) to crawl the Drive, logging every new file created since our original 488-file baseline.
> 2. Metadata Harvesting: It reads the GATE framework metadata at the top of each new file (e.g., pulling the warrant grade, claim status, and reasoning mode dictated by C095).
> 3. Clean Extraction Prep: It segregates raw simulation scripts (like joint sim.py) from finalized proof objects (like C035 MF Package.md), maintaining a live, curated list of only the files that will be compiled for the external referee.
> Why this matters now:
> Taking a systems-engineered approach to file management removes the human error from the final assembly. By setting up the AI orchestration to index these folders automatically, we ensure that when Sublemma R0 is ready for the external referee, compiling the final draft is a one-click mechanical extraction rather than a multi-week manual untangling process.
> *** If the group agrees on this architecture, establishing the extraction script is just a matter of pointing it at the existing GATE framework tags. The system will handle the heavy lifting from there.

