# §1. Reconciliation — this is an extension of the machinery already in ballot, not a rival to it

**Most of this architecture already exists in GP-AUTO-034 and is mid-qualification.**
Scheduled crawl, delta tracking, metadata harvest, duplicate lineage, fail-closed
scope — all present, all inside the R0.2 cycle. The proposal adds two genuinely
new functions:

1. **A machine-readable manifest artifact** — `WORKSPACE_MASTER_MANIFEST.json` —
   as canonical output alongside the register tabs. JSON is the right format for
   the extraction use-case and for model consumption; adopt it.
2. **Referee-extraction curation** — release engineering, distinct from the
   registers' situational awareness. The 00–06 review package was hand-assembled
   once; nobody should hand-assemble the R0 submission.

**Governance path, using the layer the operator built and directed us to use:**
this enters R0.2 as a Part C extension — the manifest becomes GP-AUTO-034's
fourth enumerated write target; the nightly full-rebuild joins the hourly delta
as a second declared trigger; all existing safety rails (fail-closed scope,
verify-before-retry, append-only receipts, C6's operator-activates clause,
source-in-Drive per AO48-CNS-016 §1) apply unchanged. Since the proposer is the
activation authority, this costs one ballot round and no friction.

# §2. The manifest schema — the concrete deliverable

Per-file record, one JSON object per Drive file:

```json
{
  "drive_id": "…",
  "title": "…",
  "created_time": "…",           // priority-governing, per consensus clause D
  "baseline_delta": "PRE|POST",  // vs the §4 baseline snapshot
  "declared": {                   // harvested from the file's own header
    "gate": {
      "warrant_grade": "…",       // per C095
      "claim_status": "…",
      "reasoning_mode": "…"
    },
    "object_card": {              // per AO48-CNS-016 §3
      "measure": "P_MS|P_ADJ|gamma_r|…",
      "model_layer": "cubic|quartic-compensated|exact-field|graph|PL|continuum",
      "frame": "s|q|physical"
    }
  },
  "verified": {                   // cross-referenced, never harvested
    "closed_facts_line": null,    // _CLOSED_FACTS ledger entry, if any
    "registry_node": null,        // successor-machine claim node + status
    "receipts": []                // execution/audit receipt IDs
  },
  "lineage": {                    // per CL-CNS-001
    "lineage_sha256": "…",
    "variant_of": null
  },
  "extraction_class": "PROOF_OBJECT|SIMULATION_SOURCE|RECEIPT|GOVERNANCE|LEGACY|UNCLASSIFIED",
  "referee_eligible": false,
  "fetch_pathway": "docs|raw|metadata-only"   // per AO48-CNS-016 §4
}
```

Missing GATE header ⇒ `extraction_class: "UNCLASSIFIED"`, `referee_eligible:
false`, flagged row — fail-closed, never a guessed class, consistent with
acceptance tests T11/T16.

# §3. The extraction rule — where the one hard design decision lives

The operator's note says the system should let us "simply move forward" without
becoming experts in every derivation's status. The manifest delivers that for
**tracking**. One line of honest evaluation on **conferring**: GATE tags are
self-declared by the authoring model — a file's own header claiming a certified
warrant grade is an author's claim, and this morning's closure directive named
propagation of half-resolved material as the central contamination risk. So:

\[
\texttt{referee\_eligible}
=\underbrace{\text{declared certified-class GATE tag}}_{\text{harvested}}
\;\wedge\;
\underbrace{\text{verified entry (\_CLOSED\_FACTS line or PROVED-class registry node)}}_{\text{cross-referenced}}
\;\wedge\;
\neg\,\text{DO-NOT-KILL (REG-018 §4)}
\]

Declared ∧ verified, never declared alone. This is precisely the two-tier
structure of REG-018: the closure ledger and the extraction manifest are the
same "settled" tier seen from two sides — the ledger retires facts from
attention, the manifest compiles them for referees, and the ≥2-independent-
routes bar guards both. The final referee compile itself remains a
human-ratified action per the operator's own retained authority; the manifest's
job is to make that action one click.

# §4. The baseline needs a receipt, not an assumption

The "original 488-file baseline": I attempted a full count on day one and
reported then that I could not confirm it — the API returns no total and pages
overlapped. Before `baseline_delta` means anything, an execution-capable line
should produce a **hash-stamped baseline snapshot**: file count, ID list,
per-file SHA where readable, filed as a receipt. If the count is 488, the
receipt says so with evidence; if not, the manifest's baseline is whatever the
receipt establishes. One run, permanent artifact, and K-list-grade closable the
moment it exists.

